## 6.1 Seed data to create

Every user-facing feature in this slice must include realistic seed data so the sandbox is demonstrable, not blank.

- Create or update Laravel seeder classes for this slice.
- Prefer multiple focused seeder classes so test data is maintainable: users/roles, org/tenant structure, feature records, edge states, and relationship/linkage records.
- Seed at least 10 realistic records for each feature introduced or changed by this slice, unless the domain has fewer valid states.
- Seed every role/persona required to test this slice's flow and the full app journey, including admin, manager/approver, regular member, and restricted/read-only identities where the domain supports them.
- Include enough record states to make the UI obvious during review, such as draft, active, approved, rejected, overdue, archived, failed, or escalated where applicable.
- The first browser review after `php artisan migrate:fresh --seed` must show populated records, not empty states, on the primary app screens.
- Update `docs/user-manual/seed-data.md` with seeded records, credentials, reset commands, and removal/production notes.

## 6.2 Seeded test credentials

If this slice creates or modifies auth, navigation, layout, middleware, users, roles, permissions, tenancy, or any user-visible workflow, implement or preserve seeded test credentials for full-flow browser QA:

- Create seeded users for every role, persona, department, tenant, permission level, approval state, or ownership path needed to test the whole app flow.
- Use real login paths. Reviewers must sign in with seeded email/username and password credentials, not bypass auth through impersonation or switching UI.
- Include credentials for both happy-path and restricted/edge-case users, such as admin, manager/approver, standard member, read-only/restricted, suspended/inactive, cross-tenant/department-denied, or domain-specific actors where applicable.
- Seed records owned by those users so dashboards, lists, approvals, notifications, policies, and cross-role handoffs can be tested immediately after `php artisan migrate:fresh --seed`.
- Document every seeded credential, role, permissions scope, and recommended test flow in `docs/user-manual/seed-data.md`.
- Do not add a navbar impersonation/user-switching UI unless the product requirements explicitly ask for one.

